WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:00.000


00:00.000 --> 00:00.000


00:00.000 --> 00:00.000


00:00.000 --> 00:00.000


00:00.450 --> 00:05.420
<b>Thou Shalt Not Die</b>

00:05.430 --> 00:06.840
A transaction.

00:06.840 --> 00:09.270
Use the healing ability for me.

00:09.270 --> 00:12.690
In exchange, I'll provide information that
 will lead to the Agency's restoration.

00:13.080 --> 00:14.660
<i>We'll meet in twenty minutes.</i>

00:14.660 --> 00:16.060
<i>At Goban Street.</i>

00:16.620 --> 00:19.120
Information that'll lead to 
the Agency's restoration!

00:19.120 --> 00:20.590
Now we have some hope.

00:20.590 --> 00:21.930
Odd.

00:22.510 --> 00:25.340
How did he discover this hideout?

00:25.340 --> 00:28.560
He must have used his 
Eyes of God or whatever, right?

00:28.560 --> 00:29.610
That's the thing.

00:30.050 --> 00:32.400
If he was able to discover this hideout,

00:32.400 --> 00:35.550
he might as well have done business 
with the Military Police instead.

00:35.850 --> 00:39.470
It would have been more profitable to 
do the formidable Hunting Dogs a favor,

00:39.470 --> 00:41.510
as opposed to the weakened Detective Agency.

00:42.050 --> 00:47.610
The Francis I know always sides with 
the stronger, more bullish side.

00:48.960 --> 00:52.770
This transaction may be a trap.

02:30.300 --> 02:32.750
Yosano-san, where are you going?

02:33.750 --> 02:35.560
To complete the transaction?

02:36.900 --> 02:38.340
It might be a trap.

02:38.340 --> 02:39.120
Why?

02:41.160 --> 02:44.100
Are you that reluctant 
to join the Port Mafia?

02:49.090 --> 02:50.850
Don't give me that bullshit!

02:50.850 --> 02:54.910
You can't help us prove 
the Agency's innocence?

02:54.910 --> 02:55.880
That is correct.

02:55.880 --> 02:57.960
The agreement with Fukuzawa-dono

02:57.960 --> 03:00.530
was that we would only help the Agency

03:00.530 --> 03:04.080
in exchange for transferring one 
of its members to the Mafia.

03:04.080 --> 03:06.490
Transfer a member of the Agency?

03:06.490 --> 03:07.850
Do you think you're funny?

03:07.850 --> 03:11.500
All you really want is for me 
to join the Mafia, don't you?

03:13.700 --> 03:16.220
In that case, I'll join the Mafia.

03:16.730 --> 03:20.620
My ability, Light Snow, 
ought to be useful to them.

03:21.010 --> 03:23.520
So please, tell me why.

03:23.520 --> 03:26.670
What happened between 
you and the Mafia boss?

03:27.580 --> 03:31.540
Does it have something to 
do with the "angel of death"

03:31.540 --> 03:33.410
that the Hunting Dogs were talking about?

03:36.650 --> 03:40.250
I guess I shouldn't trouble you any more.

03:40.960 --> 03:41.940
Fine.

03:41.940 --> 03:43.890
I'll tell you as we walk.

03:46.900 --> 03:49.540
A long time ago, the boss and Mori-sensei

03:49.540 --> 03:51.960
were close allies in the 
tripartite framework.

03:52.280 --> 03:54.700
Now, though, they're enemies.

03:54.700 --> 03:56.240
Why do you think that is?

03:56.240 --> 03:57.890
Come to think of it...

04:04.800 --> 04:08.310
<b>Episode 46</b>

04:04.800 --> 04:08.310
<b>A Dream of Butterflies</b>

04:05.020 --> 04:06.950
It's because of me.

04:09.260 --> 04:12.770
<b>Fourteen years ago
Near the end of the great war</b>

04:13.420 --> 04:16.530
An island, Tokoyamijima, appeared 
out of nowhere in the Pacific.

04:16.530 --> 04:21.060
An unclaimed island where
 it was only ever night,

04:21.060 --> 04:23.860
it became the main battleground 
towards the end of the great war.

04:24.190 --> 04:28.730
Electromagnetic waves from the aurora 
destroyed electronic equipment,

04:28.730 --> 04:32.100
resulting in pre-modern 
close-quarters combat.

04:42.270 --> 04:45.500
Don't just lie there, you lousy soldiers!

04:45.820 --> 04:49.730
Special ability: Thou Shalt Not Die.

04:47.260 --> 04:50.810
<b>Thou Shalt Not Die</b>

05:01.830 --> 05:02.880
It doesn't hurt!

05:02.880 --> 05:03.990
I can see!

05:03.990 --> 05:05.340
My eyes are working!

05:05.340 --> 05:06.440
My leg...

05:06.440 --> 05:07.640
I have my leg!

05:07.640 --> 05:09.920
You get hurt because you're weak.

05:09.920 --> 05:12.160
Get back to the damn front!

05:12.370 --> 05:17.670
<b>National
 Guard 
Infantry
 Unit 356</b>

05:12.370 --> 05:17.670
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 290 0 290

05:12.370 --> 05:17.670
<b>Sponsored 
Student
 Medic 




Yosano Akiko 
(11 years old)</b>

05:17.830 --> 05:23.170
<b>National
 Guard
 Infantry 
Unit 356</b>

05:17.830 --> 05:23.170
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 290 0 290

05:17.830 --> 05:23.170
<b>Unit Chief 
Medic Adjutant</b>

05:17.830 --> 05:23.170
<b>Mori Ougai 
(26 years old)</b>

05:23.380 --> 05:25.280
Amazing! It's a miracle.

05:25.280 --> 05:27.250
You are our god!

05:27.250 --> 05:28.590
Our savior!

05:28.590 --> 05:30.780
Let us use your likeness as our emblem!

05:30.780 --> 05:33.060
Please! Let us worship you!

05:33.060 --> 05:33.940
Go away!

05:33.940 --> 05:35.220
Piss off!

05:36.560 --> 05:40.310
Are you that enamored with my Yosano-kun?

05:40.600 --> 05:42.910
Ch-Chief Mori...

05:42.910 --> 05:44.570
We would never...

05:44.570 --> 05:46.870
Oh, shit... He's gonna kill us!

05:46.870 --> 05:48.740
He's going to pickle our organs.

05:48.740 --> 05:50.930
"Your" Yosano-kun?

05:50.930 --> 05:54.120
Since when was I yours, Mori-sensei?

05:54.480 --> 05:56.040
I'll bite your ears off.

05:56.040 --> 05:58.560
I'm your superior, am I not?

05:58.560 --> 06:02.770
I have the right to correct your 
attitude and language, too.

06:02.770 --> 06:05.180
I don't care about military policy.

06:05.180 --> 06:08.280
I was working at a candy 
shop until last week,

06:08.280 --> 06:10.790
when you dragged me out 
here against my will.

06:18.230 --> 06:19.890
She's so strong willed...

06:19.890 --> 06:20.770
I like!

06:28.360 --> 06:31.190
Reading a novel? 
Right after you nearly died?

06:32.920 --> 06:34.460
It's not a novel.

06:34.460 --> 06:36.040
It's a poetry collection.

06:37.720 --> 06:38.960
Unbelievable.

06:38.960 --> 06:41.930
I'm not telling you to 
thank me with tears of joy,

06:41.930 --> 06:45.290
but don't you have any intention 
of hurrying back to the front,

06:45.290 --> 06:46.850
now that you're all better?

06:47.510 --> 06:48.800
I thank you, for sure.

06:49.190 --> 06:51.080
That's why I want you to have this.

06:54.930 --> 06:57.210
My butterfly.

06:58.770 --> 07:00.010
<i>No.</i>

07:00.010 --> 07:00.950
<i>It's...</i>

07:01.750 --> 07:03.310
<i>Metal?</i>

07:03.590 --> 07:05.920
Thank you, angel.

07:07.540 --> 07:09.030
A-Angel?!

07:13.640 --> 07:16.830
But how did you do that just now?

07:16.830 --> 07:18.740
Was that your special ability?

07:19.050 --> 07:21.390
It's not much of an ability.

07:21.390 --> 07:24.660
It's not going to change 
the world, like yours can.

07:25.020 --> 07:26.940
Me? Change the world?

07:26.940 --> 07:28.720
You're joking.

07:29.250 --> 07:31.810
There are some things you notice 
because you're just a private.

07:32.630 --> 07:34.280
The Special Ability Doctrine.

07:35.380 --> 07:38.440
The great powers of Europe 
that started the Gifted wars

07:38.440 --> 07:40.810
are changing the very concept of war.

07:40.810 --> 07:47.660
If we are to prevail, we must prove this 
to the military brass as fast as possible.

07:47.970 --> 07:51.790
That's why Chief Mori 
brought you into the unit.

07:53.450 --> 07:56.760
Isn't that right, Chief Mori?

07:57.740 --> 08:01.990
I see you've read my 
Immortal Regiment paper.

08:02.490 --> 08:03.840
What are you talking about?!

08:04.110 --> 08:07.150
I was certain that was a 
classified military document.

08:07.150 --> 08:10.190
Military brass? Immortal? 
What the hell are you talking about?

08:10.190 --> 08:13.420
I just came here to save people's lives!

08:13.420 --> 08:15.170
Let's go, Yosano.

08:15.580 --> 08:18.040
There are more patients waiting.

08:18.690 --> 08:21.670
Elise-chan, the next chart, please.

08:22.750 --> 08:24.740
Yes, master.

08:28.910 --> 08:29.900
Dammit...

08:29.900 --> 08:32.360
Those assholes have set up camp so close.

08:32.360 --> 08:34.360
They don't think we're a threat.

08:34.360 --> 08:36.320
I hate to admit it, but we aren't.

08:36.650 --> 08:39.780
We don't even have weapons 
that can reach that far.

08:39.780 --> 08:42.970
We're way outgunned and outnumbered.

08:43.440 --> 08:45.110
Unless something changes...

08:45.110 --> 08:46.910
We'll take them down!

08:46.910 --> 08:49.350
We have an angel on our side.

08:49.350 --> 08:50.580
You're right.

08:58.090 --> 08:58.980
Shit!

09:00.270 --> 09:01.620
Everyone, get down!

09:27.470 --> 09:28.760
I have my right arm.

09:29.280 --> 09:30.980
Are you feeling all right?

09:38.150 --> 09:40.950
You look pretty exhausted yourself.

09:40.950 --> 09:42.670
Of course I do.

09:42.670 --> 09:45.310
I treated 80 people all at once.

09:45.310 --> 09:48.760
The worst one had half his body blown off.

09:49.480 --> 09:54.120
I could heal his wounds with my ability, 
but I couldn't heal his mind.

09:54.580 --> 09:57.340
He can't even say his name.

09:57.340 --> 09:58.790
What about everyone else?

09:58.790 --> 10:01.500
The ones who didn't die 
went back to the front.

10:01.500 --> 10:03.160
They're lacking men.

10:06.520 --> 10:08.250
"Angel," my ass.

10:08.250 --> 10:11.440
I'm basically healing them 
just for them to die again.

10:12.410 --> 10:13.490
You're wrong.

10:19.350 --> 10:20.580
What's that?

10:20.580 --> 10:22.760
I'm keeping count.

10:23.230 --> 10:25.850
Of the number of times you've saved my life.

10:26.550 --> 10:28.480
Today makes the fifth time.

10:28.910 --> 10:31.670
I happen to like tallying with 
the character for "true."

10:32.320 --> 10:36.200
Every time I count something 
and I finish writing "true,"

10:36.200 --> 10:39.900
I get the sense that something 
<i>just</i> was created in the world.

10:40.580 --> 10:42.600
This is your justness.

10:42.940 --> 10:44.450
If it weren't for you,

10:44.450 --> 10:47.530
I would never have had a chance to 
meet my parents and brother again.

10:48.860 --> 10:50.730
I'm glad you're here.

10:54.700 --> 10:55.910
Thanks.

10:56.830 --> 10:59.740
Actually, I...

10:59.740 --> 11:01.140
Hey, private first-class!

11:01.550 --> 11:03.490
The front is in a dire situation.

11:03.490 --> 11:05.320
You're all better, so get back out there!

11:05.320 --> 11:06.300
Yes, sir.

11:12.840 --> 11:19.230
But as if to laugh in the face of our efforts,
 the situation continued to worsen.

11:20.140 --> 11:24.080
I was treating soldiers 
once every three days.

11:24.470 --> 11:26.380
Then once every day.

11:26.380 --> 11:29.580
Soon, three times a day.

11:29.890 --> 11:33.590
It was no longer correct 
to even call it a war.

11:34.240 --> 11:36.540
We were just standing there, 
being brutalized.

11:37.050 --> 11:41.070
A normal unit would have given 
up and retreated long ago,

11:42.370 --> 11:44.640
but that never happened.

11:45.390 --> 11:46.980
Because I was there.

11:48.890 --> 11:51.650
It hurts... It hurts...

11:50.810 --> 11:53.380
My leg... My leg!

11:53.380 --> 11:54.450
I can't fight anymore...

11:54.450 --> 11:55.600
Spare me...

11:55.600 --> 11:56.430
No more...

11:56.430 --> 11:58.670
I don't want to go to the front anymore...

11:59.110 --> 12:01.480
That's a fracture of the right radius.

12:03.260 --> 12:04.620
Treatment.

12:04.620 --> 12:07.300
Dad... Mom...

12:07.920 --> 12:09.240
I'll be home soon...

12:12.440 --> 12:13.870
I don't want to fix them.

12:14.530 --> 12:16.890
You're going to abandon his wounds?

12:16.890 --> 12:18.880
Yeah. That's right.

12:18.880 --> 12:21.500
Let him fall back and get 
treatment on his own!

12:22.120 --> 12:23.360
I see.

12:24.110 --> 12:27.640
You want to free him from the battlefield.

12:29.530 --> 12:31.440
What a conundrum.

12:31.690 --> 12:35.370
I'm obliged to give you orders,

12:35.370 --> 12:38.780
but I have a hard time saying 
no to a girl's wishes...

12:38.780 --> 12:40.680
Not yours, though.

12:40.680 --> 12:41.370
Do it.

12:43.210 --> 12:45.200
You know of the samurai, don't you?

12:46.350 --> 12:50.530
They failed to understand war by 
gun and cannon, and perished.

12:52.480 --> 12:56.480
In the war after, the nation that recognized 
 tanks as beasts that could ravage

12:56.480 --> 13:02.010
enemy territory, not as simple turrets,
 massacred the enemy.

13:02.760 --> 13:05.330
In naval battles, the nation 
that failed to realize

13:05.330 --> 13:08.630
that planes would be the masters 
of the sea was the one to fall.

13:08.630 --> 13:12.370
And now, special abilities are changing war.

13:12.780 --> 13:16.180
Your role is to make the 
military understand change.

13:16.450 --> 13:17.280
Do it.

13:17.280 --> 13:19.280
Or else the nation will fall.

13:19.280 --> 13:20.230
I refuse!

13:20.570 --> 13:23.940
I just want to save the 
lives in front of me!

13:27.110 --> 13:28.150
Very well.

13:34.370 --> 13:35.380
There.

13:35.850 --> 13:37.190
He's dying.

13:37.790 --> 13:38.910
Fix him.

13:44.870 --> 13:47.660
No one could leave the battlefield.

13:49.320 --> 13:52.460
The soldier who drew a picture of me,

13:52.460 --> 13:55.940
the soldier who pat my head, 
saying I reminded him of his sister,

13:55.940 --> 13:58.840
the soldier who made me delicious coffee...

13:58.840 --> 14:00.190
They all died.

14:00.910 --> 14:05.530
If it weren't for me, they could 
have left with mere injuries.

14:06.610 --> 14:08.560
Do you know the word "annihilation"?

14:09.160 --> 14:13.890
It's used when half of a 
unit is incapacitated.

14:13.890 --> 14:16.070
Not when half of the unit is <i>dead</i>.

14:16.560 --> 14:21.440
In other words, if half of an army is hurt,
 it retreats and the battle ends.

14:22.060 --> 14:25.790
But as long as I was there, 
there was no retreat.

14:25.790 --> 14:27.540
That's why they couldn't lose.

14:28.330 --> 14:30.910
To lose is a human right,

14:30.910 --> 14:33.580
but I took that from them.

14:34.260 --> 14:38.500
Deprived of the ability to lose, 
there's only one place a military can go.

14:39.500 --> 14:40.460
Stop him!

14:40.460 --> 14:41.480
Take his dagger!

14:41.480 --> 14:43.350
Everyone's going to die 
because of that bitch!

14:43.630 --> 14:46.230
This isn't a war!

14:46.230 --> 14:47.470
Let me go, asshole!

14:47.470 --> 14:49.850
Let me go! Let me go!

14:51.250 --> 14:56.870
It happened on the day a soldier 
I was close to tried to kill me.

15:04.910 --> 15:06.640
My hair ornament's missing.

15:07.800 --> 15:09.750
I must have dropped it somewhere.

15:10.280 --> 15:12.230
I can't lose it after he gave it to me.

15:13.490 --> 15:15.240
I have to find it.

15:16.500 --> 15:17.770
Yosano-san,

15:18.990 --> 15:21.140
I'd like to ask you to deliver a message.

15:21.500 --> 15:22.900
That voice...

15:23.260 --> 15:25.160
I promised I'd endure...

15:25.160 --> 15:29.910
But your ability, the justness 
of it, has taught me...

15:30.900 --> 15:33.740
Everyone has their limits.

15:34.980 --> 15:37.530
Remember how I called you an angel?

15:38.690 --> 15:41.140
You're more than that.

15:41.140 --> 15:43.590
You've descended on the battlefield

15:43.820 --> 15:45.480
as an angel of death.

15:46.300 --> 15:49.250
Please tell my family that I said goodbye.

16:19.790 --> 16:22.000
<b><i>You are too just</i></b>

16:26.060 --> 16:30.590
<b><i>You are too just</i></b>

16:30.590 --> 16:33.550
<b><i>You are too just</i></b>

16:43.350 --> 16:47.740
My memory after that 
point is honestly vague.

16:48.020 --> 16:49.030
From what I've heard,

16:49.030 --> 16:53.880
I was arrested for setting explosives 
to try to blow up the carrier.

16:55.390 --> 16:58.460
Even after the war, I was kept 
in isolation in a facility.

16:59.090 --> 17:04.000
Not that I imagine I would have left,
 even if the door was open.

17:04.730 --> 17:09.450
So it was the Agency that rescued you?

17:09.450 --> 17:12.000
If only that were the case.

17:12.000 --> 17:15.550
It was the worst person imaginable who did.

17:16.000 --> 17:18.960
It was three years after the war ended.

17:29.180 --> 17:30.900
I finally found you.

17:36.320 --> 17:39.810
I need your ability again.

17:49.510 --> 17:52.540
You would drag her back into hell again?!

17:52.540 --> 17:55.210
Are you playing the part 
of a devil, Mori-sensei?!

17:55.490 --> 18:00.090
She is the very pillar of the 
tripartite framework, of the city's peace.

18:00.350 --> 18:03.750
An immortal army, led by Yosano-kun,

18:03.750 --> 18:06.940
is best suited to defeating 
the formidable Port Mafia boss!

18:09.990 --> 18:11.930
"Best suited," my ass!

18:11.930 --> 18:13.820
Your reasoning lacks humanity!

18:14.940 --> 18:16.030
Humanity?!

18:16.330 --> 18:19.940
War is a game in which the first to 
take humanity into account loses!

18:20.770 --> 18:24.180
Then our alliance ends today!

18:24.180 --> 18:26.730
In fact, it's your life that ends today!

18:34.630 --> 18:36.630
Sheesh, nasty.

18:36.630 --> 18:39.260
Grown-up fights are always so pompous.

18:40.180 --> 18:42.010
Oh, this?

18:42.430 --> 18:45.600
I'm freeing you while the boss is fighting.

18:45.600 --> 18:46.770
That's the plan.

18:47.280 --> 18:48.530
Take me back.

18:50.480 --> 18:51.830
Take me back.

18:51.830 --> 18:54.380
I can't go outside.

18:54.380 --> 18:55.350
Why not?

18:55.950 --> 19:00.100
My special ability makes 
it too easy to save lives.

19:00.100 --> 19:04.440
I make the lives of everyone
 around me seem cheap.

19:04.890 --> 19:07.870
I can't be allowed to live.

19:09.530 --> 19:11.040
That's so stupid.

19:11.680 --> 19:13.860
I don't give a crap.

19:14.360 --> 19:17.350
Why don't you give up using 
your special ability, then?

19:17.350 --> 19:19.320
If I could do that...

19:19.320 --> 19:21.230
You're saying you can't?

19:21.230 --> 19:22.370
Why not?

19:22.370 --> 19:25.090
Because you have a crazy healing ability?

19:25.090 --> 19:28.140
Because everyone tried to use your ability?

19:30.360 --> 19:31.560
Nope.

19:31.560 --> 19:34.630
My superhuman deduction is the 
best special ability in the world.

19:34.630 --> 19:36.800
No other ability matters.

19:37.300 --> 19:40.000
With me on your side, 
I can solve all your problems!

19:41.950 --> 19:45.060
If you doubt my abilities, 
I can prove it to you.

19:57.300 --> 19:58.410
It's...

19:59.430 --> 20:00.450
How?

20:01.230 --> 20:03.930
I never told anyone about this!

20:04.510 --> 20:06.710
I found it on an old carrier.

20:07.360 --> 20:08.540
See?

20:08.540 --> 20:10.480
I know everything.

20:10.480 --> 20:12.480
Try asking me a question.

20:12.480 --> 20:13.950
I'll answer anything..

20:15.650 --> 20:19.720
Then... What should I do now?

20:20.390 --> 20:23.000
The people I cared about died because of me.

20:23.690 --> 20:25.610
That's how it's always going to be.

20:26.010 --> 20:31.800
There will always be people who want 
to use my ability against my will.

20:27.600 --> 20:28.470
<b><i>You are too just</i></b>

20:28.470 --> 20:30.220
<b><i>You are too just</i></b>

20:32.310 --> 20:35.450
Is there really anywhere 
I can be allowed to live?

20:36.930 --> 20:37.770
There is.

20:40.560 --> 20:45.200
There's just one place in the 
world that doesn't need you.

20:46.430 --> 20:48.760
Join the Armed Detective Agency.

20:49.380 --> 20:51.460
We don't want your special ability.

20:52.010 --> 20:54.100
We want that kindness of yours.

20:54.890 --> 20:57.130
You didn't want anyone to die, did you?

20:57.740 --> 20:59.790
That's why you're in so much pain.

21:00.460 --> 21:03.520
I want to invite you because 
you have such kindness.

21:04.360 --> 21:06.270
I don't care about your ability.

21:06.990 --> 21:09.960
It's your kindness that means something.

21:21.080 --> 21:23.120
Yosano-san, what's wrong?

21:26.140 --> 21:27.510
Nothing.

21:29.340 --> 21:30.880
Let's go.

21:30.880 --> 21:33.630
